---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../../components/ContactCTA.astro';

const title = 'Albert Lea, Minnesota Drain Cleaning | A-1 Drain Cleaning';
const description = 'A-1 Drain Cleaning serves Albert Lea, Minnesota for clogged drains, main drain backups, floor drain problems and sewer-line blockages. Call 641-530-2728.';
---

<MainLayout title={title} description={description} path="/albert-lea-mn-drain-cleaning/">
  <Header />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="bg-[#1A1A68] text-white">
      <div class="container grid gap-10 py-14 sm:py-18 lg:grid-cols-[1.15fr_.85fr] lg:items-center lg:py-20">
        <div>
          <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-300">
            <a href="/" class="hover:text-white">Home</a>
            <span class="mx-2" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
            <span class="text-white">Albert Lea, Minnesota</span>
          </nav>
          <p class="mt-5 text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-red-300">A-1 Drain Cleaning • Albert Lea, Minnesota</p>
          <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-4xl text-5xl font-black leading-[.98] tracking-tight sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl">Albert Lea Drain Cleaning</h1>
          <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-200 sm:text-xl">A-1 Drain Cleaning serves Albert Lea for clogged drains, main drain backups, floor drain problems, laundry drain trouble, and sewer-line blockages.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-7 text-slate-200">If one fixture is slow, several fixtures are backing up, or wastewater is coming up through a low drain, tell us what the water is doing. That pattern helps narrow down where the restriction may be.</p>
          <a href="tel:+16415302728" class="mt-8 inline-block rounded-md bg-[#c52b34] px-7 py-4 text-center text-lg font-black text-white hover:bg-[#a82129]">CALL 641-530-2728</a>
          <p class="mt-5 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-300">A-1 Drain Cleaning is based in Mason City, Iowa.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="border border-white/15 bg-white/10 p-6 sm:p-8" aria-labelledby="albert-lea-problem">
          <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-red-200">Start with the symptom</p>
          <h2 id="albert-lea-problem" class="mt-3 text-3xl font-black leading-tight">What is the drain doing?</h2>
          <ul class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-slate-200">
            <li class="border-b border-white/10 pb-4"><strong class="text-white">One fixture:</strong> a sink, tub, shower, or toilet is slow or stopped.</li>
            <li class="border-b border-white/10 pb-4"><strong class="text-white">Several fixtures:</strong> more than one drain backs up or gurgles.</li>
            <li class="border-b border-white/10 pb-4"><strong class="text-white">Low drain:</strong> wastewater rises through a floor drain or another low opening.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Laundry:</strong> washer discharge backs up through a standpipe or nearby drain.</li>
          </ul>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-white py-14 sm:py-18" aria-labelledby="albert-lea-answers">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Albert Lea drain problems</p>
        <h2 id="albert-lea-answers" class="mt-2 max-w-4xl text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-4xl">Common drain and sewer problems</h2>
        <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">The symptom matters. One slow sink can be a local fixture or branch-drain problem. When several fixtures are affected, a toilet flush makes another drain rise, or wastewater comes up through a low drain, the restriction may be farther down a shared line or the main sewer.</p>
        <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Main drain backup</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">When toilets, sinks, tubs, or other fixtures are affected together, the restriction may be in the main drain or a shared line.</p><a href="/services/main-drain-cleaning/" class="mt-4 inline-flex font-black text-[#b4232b] underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4">Main drain cleaning →</a></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Floor drain backup</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">Wastewater rising through a low drain can be a sign that a downstream line cannot carry water away fast enough.</p><a href="/services/basement-floor-drains/" class="mt-4 inline-flex font-black text-[#b4232b] underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4">Floor drain service →</a></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Sewer line blockage</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">A restriction farther down the sewer line can affect multiple fixtures and cause recurring backups.</p><a href="/services/sewer-line-cleaning/" class="mt-4 inline-flex font-black text-[#b4232b] underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4">Sewer line cleaning →</a></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Kitchen and bathroom drains</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">Slow or stopped sinks, tubs, and showers can have a blockage in the fixture drain or nearby branch line.</p><a href="/services/kitchen-drains/" class="mt-4 inline-flex font-black text-[#b4232b] underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4">Kitchen drains →</a><a href="/services/bathroom-shower-drains/" class="mt-2 inline-flex font-black text-[#b4232b] underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4">Bathroom &amp; shower drains →</a></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Laundry drain backup</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">A washing machine pumps out quickly. A restricted laundry or shared drain can cause water to rise when the washer empties.</p><a href="/services/laundry-drains/" class="mt-4 inline-flex font-black text-[#b4232b] underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4">Laundry drains →</a></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Tree roots in sewer lines</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">Roots entering a sewer line can contribute to recurring blockages. If the same line keeps stopping up, mention that history.</p><a href="/services/tree-roots-in-sewer-line/" class="mt-4 inline-flex font-black text-[#b4232b] underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4">Tree roots in sewer lines →</a></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-slate-100 py-14 sm:py-18" aria-labelledby="albert-lea-quick-answers">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Quick answers</p>
        <h2 id="albert-lea-quick-answers" class="mt-2 max-w-4xl text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-4xl">Albert Lea drain cleaning questions</h2>
        <div class="mt-8 space-y-4">
          <article class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">How do I know if the main drain is blocked?</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-4xl leading-7 text-slate-700">Several fixtures backing up together, one fixture causing another to rise, or wastewater appearing at a low drain can point to a restriction farther down the drain system. Those symptoms are clues, not a diagnosis.</p></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">What should I do if wastewater comes up through a floor drain?</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-4xl leading-7 text-slate-700">Stop using toilets, sinks, showers, and the washing machine as much as practical. Keep children and pets away from wastewater. Call A-1 Drain Cleaning at <a href="tel:+16415302728" class="font-bold text-[#b4232b] underline underline-offset-2">641-530-2728</a> and explain which fixtures were being used when the backup happened.</p></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Why does my washing machine make another drain back up?</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-4xl leading-7 text-slate-700">A washer releases a large amount of water quickly. If the laundry drain or a shared line cannot carry that flow away, water can rise in the standpipe or come through a nearby low drain.</p></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Can a sewer backup affect more than one fixture?</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-4xl leading-7 text-slate-700">Yes. A restriction in a shared drain or main sewer can affect several fixtures. Tell us which fixture backs up first and whether flushing, showering, or laundry changes the symptoms.</p></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Do you provide 24/7 drain and sewer service?</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-4xl leading-7 text-slate-700">A-1 Drain Cleaning offers 24/7 drain and sewer service. Call <a href="tel:+16415302728" class="font-bold text-[#b4232b] underline underline-offset-2">641-530-2728</a> and explain the blockage or backup.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-white py-14 sm:py-18" aria-labelledby="albert-lea-local">
      <div class="container grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.2fr] lg:items-start">
        <div>
          <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Albert Lea, MN</p>
          <h2 id="albert-lea-local" class="mt-2 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-4xl">Albert Lea, MN</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl leading-7 text-slate-700">A-1 Drain Cleaning is based in Mason City, Iowa and serves Albert Lea customers for drain and sewer problems. This is a service-area page, not a claim that A-1 Drain Cleaning has a physical office in Minnesota.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl leading-7 text-slate-700">When you call, give us the Albert Lea address and describe what is backing up. If several fixtures are involved, say which one showed the problem first.</p>
          <a href="tel:+16415302728" class="mt-6 inline-flex rounded-md bg-[#c52b34] px-6 py-3 font-black text-white hover:bg-[#a82129]">CALL 641-530-2728</a>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <a href="/services/main-drain-cleaning/" class="border border-slate-200 p-4 font-black text-slate-950 hover:border-[#b4232b] hover:text-[#b4232b]">Main drain cleaning</a>
          <a href="/services/sewer-line-cleaning/" class="border border-slate-200 p-4 font-black text-slate-950 hover:border-[#b4232b] hover:text-[#b4232b]">Sewer line cleaning</a>
          <a href="/services/basement-floor-drains/" class="border border-slate-200 p-4 font-black text-slate-950 hover:border-[#b4232b] hover:text-[#b4232b]">Floor drain service</a>
          <a href="/services/laundry-drains/" class="border border-slate-200 p-4 font-black text-slate-950 hover:border-[#b4232b] hover:text-[#b4232b]">Laundry drains</a>
          <a href="/services/kitchen-drains/" class="border border-slate-200 p-4 font-black text-slate-950 hover:border-[#b4232b] hover:text-[#b4232b]">Kitchen drains</a>
          <a href="/services/tree-roots-in-sewer-line/" class="border border-slate-200 p-4 font-black text-slate-950 hover:border-[#b4232b] hover:text-[#b4232b]">Tree roots in sewer lines</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <ContactCTA showForm />
  </main>
  <Footer />
</MainLayout>
